.TH FBSET 1 "July 25, 2026"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
fbset \- inspect or change a ReBSD DRM framebuffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fbset
[
.I WIDTHxHEIGHT
]
.PP
.B fbset
[
.I width height
]
.PP
.B fbset
.B fill
.I pixel-value
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fbset
queries or changes the active DRM framebuffer mode through
.IR /dev/fb0 .
It uses the same interface on every supported platform.
The utility also queries the Linux fbdev compatibility view and verifies that
its geometry, stride, physical address, and framebuffer length agree with the
native ReBSD DRM information.
.PP
With no arguments,
.B fbset
prints the current geometry, pixel format, framebuffer address, mode index,
pixel clock, and mapping information.
.PP
The
.B fill
form fills the current framebuffer with the supplied native pixel value
through the shared mapping returned by
.IR /dev/fb0 .
This is a direct mapping smoke test, not a write(2) transfer.
.PP
The Ci20 driver currently exposes 640x480 XRGB8888.  The N64 driver exposes
320x240 RGBA5551 and, when framebuffer memory permits, 640x480 interlaced
RGBA5551.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the current framebuffer mode:
.PP
.RS
.nf
fbset
.fi
.RE
.PP
Select an advertised 640x480 mode:
.PP
.RS
.nf
fbset 640x480
.fi
.RE
.PP
Fill an RGBA5551 framebuffer with blue, or an XRGB8888 framebuffer with red:
.PP
.RS
.nf
fbset fill 0x001f
fbset fill 0x00ff0000
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP 12
.I /dev/fb0
ReBSD DRM framebuffer device with Linux fbdev compatibility
